1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,032
This is RoomEQ.

2
00:00:01,032 --> 00:00:04,680
It tunes a home audio system to the room it lives in.

3
00:00:04,680 --> 00:00:13,765
It measures the room with an iPhone microphone, works out a parametric E Q, and applies it in real time to everything the Mac plays.

4
00:00:13,765 --> 00:00:16,655
Every part of it runs locally, on the Mac.

5
00:00:17,008 --> 00:00:21,477
For this tour it runs in demo mode, shown by the blue badge at the top.

6
00:00:21,477 --> 00:00:25,693
The audio engine, the solver and this dashboard are the real thing.

7
00:00:25,693 --> 00:00:27,959
Only the outside world is simulated.

8
00:00:27,959 --> 00:00:36,330
A music source, a small living room with a two point one speaker system, and a virtual phone that follows the instructions on screen.

9
00:00:36,682 --> 00:00:38,995
The top bar controls the live audio.

10
00:00:38,995 --> 00:00:41,950
E Q on, or bypass, for a quick A B comparison.

11
00:00:41,950 --> 00:00:46,062
Bypass keeps the same preamp, so you compare tone, not loudness.

12
00:00:46,062 --> 00:00:49,917
A volume trim, and live meters for the input and the output.

13
00:00:49,917 --> 00:00:57,241
Next to them, the limiter, the added latency, the clock drift between the two audio devices, and a glitch counter.

14
00:00:57,594 --> 00:01:02,275
Safety comes first, because a bad filter should never blast the speakers.

15
00:01:02,275 --> 00:01:08,816
The panic button, or the space bar, bypasses the E Q instantly and drops the level by twenty decibels.

16
00:01:08,816 --> 00:01:11,574
Press it again and the sound fades back in.

17
00:01:11,574 --> 00:01:15,935
Behind it sits a look-ahead limiter that never lets the output clip.

18
00:01:16,288 --> 00:01:18,062
Measuring starts down here.

19
00:01:18,062 --> 00:01:21,938
On a real setup you scan this card's code with your iPhone.

20
00:01:21,938 --> 00:01:32,974
The phone opens a small web page, and streams raw microphone audio to the Mac over Wi-Fi, with echo cancellation, noise suppression and automatic gain all switched off.

21
00:01:32,974 --> 00:01:35,930
Here, the virtual phone is already connected.

22
00:01:36,282 --> 00:01:39,272
This is the page the phone sees the first time.

23
00:01:39,272 --> 00:01:48,178
Safari only allows the microphone over a secure connection, so it walks you through trusting RoomEQ's own certificate, in three short steps.

24
00:01:48,178 --> 00:01:54,921
After that, it shows a start button, a live level meter, and the instructions for each listening position.

25
00:01:55,273 --> 00:01:56,720
Now the main job, live.

26
00:01:56,720 --> 00:01:57,349
Auto-tune.

27
00:01:57,349 --> 00:02:00,242
A short burst of noise checks the level first.

28
00:02:00,242 --> 00:02:06,093
Then the Mac plays a sweep from twenty hertz to twenty kilohertz, framed by two sync markers.

29
00:02:06,093 --> 00:02:15,214
The phone and the Mac run on different clocks, so the markers also measure the clock drift, and the recording is corrected before it is analysed.

30
00:02:15,564 --> 00:02:19,147
After the first round, the solver fits up to ten filters.

31
00:02:19,147 --> 00:02:23,107
It prefers cuts over boosts, and leaves deep narrow dips alone.

32
00:02:23,107 --> 00:02:29,833
Then every listening position is measured twice, with the E Q off and with it on, without moving the phone.

33
00:02:29,833 --> 00:02:36,999
That way the improvement it reports is a fair comparison, even in a room where the bass changes from seat to seat.

34
00:02:36,999 --> 00:02:38,257
The best round wins.

35
00:02:44,669 --> 00:02:45,864
Here is the result.

36
00:02:45,864 --> 00:02:48,127
Orange is the room before, measured.

37
00:02:48,127 --> 00:02:51,334
Blue is after, also measured, through the live E Q.

38
00:02:51,334 --> 00:02:56,363
The dotted line is the target, with a gentle bass lift and a slight treble tilt.

39
00:02:56,363 --> 00:02:58,438
The bands show where it corrects.

40
00:02:58,438 --> 00:03:06,423
Fully below five hundred hertz, gently up to four kilohertz, and not at all above that, where a phone microphone is unreliable.

41
00:03:06,776 --> 00:03:12,998
Below it is the E Q the engine is applying, including the automatic preamp that keeps headroom.

42
00:03:12,998 --> 00:03:15,093
Hover anywhere for exact values.

43
00:03:15,093 --> 00:03:18,695
Every number in the chart is also available as a table.

44
00:03:22,048 --> 00:03:24,029
The filters are fully editable.

45
00:03:24,029 --> 00:03:25,435
Frequency, gain and Q.

46
00:03:25,435 --> 00:03:27,544
Let's soften this one, and apply.

47
00:03:27,544 --> 00:03:33,040
The new E Q runs silently for a moment, then crossfades in, so there is never a click.

48
00:03:33,040 --> 00:03:40,837
The chart switches to a dashed prediction until the next measurement, and values that could hurt the speakers are refused.

49
00:03:41,189 --> 00:03:43,401
Verify E Q checks the whole chain.

50
00:03:43,401 --> 00:03:46,394
Four sweeps, with the phone left in one place.

51
00:03:46,394 --> 00:03:51,663
Bypassed, through the E Q, ten decibels quieter, and once more for repeatability.

52
00:03:51,663 --> 00:03:54,526
Because nothing moves, the room cancels out.

53
00:03:54,526 --> 00:04:01,812
It proves the E Q reaches the speakers exactly as designed, and that the speaker sounds the same at both levels.

54
00:04:02,163 --> 00:04:09,653
Now a real result, from an actual living room, with an F and D two point one speaker system and an iPhone fifteen.

55
00:04:09,653 --> 00:04:12,937
Before, a bass build-up of more than ten decibels.

56
00:04:12,937 --> 00:04:17,339
After, measured through the E Q, the bass sits close to the target.

57
00:04:17,339 --> 00:04:21,741
Every result is saved as a preset, and nothing is ever overwritten.

58
00:04:22,093 --> 00:04:24,290
RoomEQ is honest about its limits.

59
00:04:24,290 --> 00:04:27,199
These notes come from the measurement itself.

60
00:04:27,199 --> 00:04:34,050
No E Q can fill a room null or fix speaker placement, and a phone microphone is rough at high frequencies.

61
00:04:34,050 --> 00:04:41,159
When the bass is simply too loud, it tells you to turn the subwoofer down on the speaker, which beats any E Q.

62
00:04:41,511 --> 00:04:51,754
Under the hood, the audio path is allocation free and compiled, with an adaptive resampler that tracks clock drift, all covered by more than seventy automated tests.

63
00:04:51,754 --> 00:04:52,188
RoomEQ.

64
00:04:52,188 --> 00:04:56,161
Measure with your phone, hear your room the way it should sound.
